      <!-- FAQ SECTION -->
      <section class="section" id="faq" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--border); padding-top: 40px; margin-top: 40px;">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
          
          <div class="box" style="margin: 0;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">1. What is the ideal pH for a car wash shampoo?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              For premium detailing, a pH of 7.0 to 7.5 (neutral) is ideal. This ensures the product is safe for all types of paint, waxes, and modern ceramic coatings while still providing enough alkalinity to emulsify organic grime.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">2. Can I use SDS in my car shampoo formulation?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              While Sodium Dodecyl Sulfate (SDS) is a powerful surfactant, it can be harsh on paint and skin. Most premium formulations prefer Sodium Laureth Sulfate (SLES) or AOS for a better balance of cleaning power and safety.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">3. Why does my car shampoo lose its viscosity over time?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              Viscosity loss is often due to temperature instability or bacterial contamination. Using high-quality rheology modifiers and a broad-spectrum preservative system is critical for industrial consistency.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">4. How important is foam in car shampoo?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              Functionally, foam helps suspend dirt and provides visual coverage. Psychologically, thick foam is associated with high concentration and quality by consumers, making it a vital marketing feature.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">5. What is the difference between car shampoo and dish soap?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              Dish soaps are designed to strip grease and often contain harsh degreasers that remove automotive waxes. Car shampoos are formulated with lubricants and neutral surfactants to protect the delicate clear coat.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">6. How do I scale up from a 10L batch to 1000L?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              Scaling up requires adjusting mixing times and using industrial equipment like high-shear emulsifiers. It is vital to maintain the same temperature profiles and addition sequences as confirmed in the lab scale.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
